 },
 "intro": {
  "title": "THE HIVE-SONG APPROACH",
  "lines": [
   "A gorge nearly three hundred metres long, and a tower at the end of it that keeps time.",
   "Six posts on the banks, a song in every one. The way to the gate is the trench and two levers."
  ]
 },
 "outro": "The drum gate turned on its two bolts and let the red in. The floor beyond it goes down in wide steps, and the light on the ribs is beating a little faster.",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "start",
   "at": [10, 30],
   "radius": 5,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "A gorge cut into pale stone, and at the far end of it a tower with a red light in it. The light comes and goes about once every second and a half."
  },
  {
   "id": "beat",
   "at": [20, 29],
   "radius": 5,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "Every rib on these banks is lit together and dimmed together. They are keeping time to the tower."
  },
  {
   "id": "count",
   "at": [26, 30],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "COUNT PLATE",
   "text": "OWED 52,310. SUNG 49,715. Under it one stroke is scratched for each night the count has been short. The strokes run off the edge of the plate."
  },
  {
   "id": "breath",
   "at": [32, 24],
   "radius": 6,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "A Chorister sings a burst and has to draw breath. Its voice breaks for about as long as it takes to say so. Move then."
  },
  {
   "id": "cover",
   "at": [48, 18],
   "radius": 6,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The crescents on the banks are stone. So are the ribs on the lip of each slope. A song does not go through either."
  },
  {
   "id": "tower",
   "at": [70, 30],
   "radius": 6,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "The tower is wider at the top than at the bottom. The red in it goes in step with the ribs, and after a while so does my pulse."
  },
  {
   "id": "relays",
   "at": [118, 31],
   "radius": 6,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The gate has two bolts, one under the last base of each bank. A brass lever on a root of black cable, under an amber lamp."
  },
  {
   "id": "gate",
   "at": [131, 30],
   "radius": 5,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The drum gate is shut. It is held by the north relay and the south relay, and it opens only when both are thrown."
  },
  {
   "id": "relay-n",
   "at": [1, 1],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "INES",
